{% set M = N.mandate %}{% set H = N.headline %}{% set U = N.cells.us_mkt %}{% set S = N.settings %}
<!doctype html>
<html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Growth with a floor: committee deck</title>
<style>
:root { --ink:#1b1f24; --muted:#5b6470; --accent:#b3346d; --rule:#d8dde3; --bg:#ffffff; }
@page { size: 13.333in 7.5in; margin: 0; }
html, body { margin:0; padding:0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink);
             font-family: "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif; }
.slide { width: 13.333in; height: 7.5in; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 0.55in 0.7in 0.45in; position: relative;
         page-break-after: always; break-after: page; overflow: hidden; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
.slide:last-child { page-break-after: auto; break-after: auto; }
h1 { font-size: 27px; line-height: 1.22; margin: 0 0 16px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; max-width: 11.6in; }
.kicker { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase;
          margin-bottom: 8px; }
.row { display: flex; gap: 0.4in; flex: 1; min-height: 0; }
.col { flex: 1; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
.wide { flex: 1.65; }
img { max-width: 100%; max-height: 4.9in; object-fit: contain; }
.big { font-size: 46px; font-weight: 750; color: var(--accent); line-height: 1; }
.bigl { font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); margin: 4px 0 18px; }
ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.4; }
li { margin: 0 0 10px; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12.5px; width: 100%; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
th { text-align: left; border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--ink); padding: 4px 6px; }
td { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 3.5px 6px; }
.src { position: absolute; bottom: 0.22in; left: 0.7in; right: 0.7in; font-size: 10px; color: var(--muted); }
.num { position: absolute; bottom: 0.22in; right: 0.7in; font-size: 10px; color: var(--muted); }
.note { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 8px; }
.title { justify-content: center; }
.title h1 { font-size: 46px; max-width: 10in; }
.title .sub { font-size: 22px; color: var(--muted); margin: 10px 0 36px; max-width: 10in; }
.box { border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); background: #fbf3f7; padding: 12px 16px; font-size: 16px; margin-top: 12px; }
</style></head><body>

<section class="slide title">
  <div class="kicker">Investment committee · MIT 15.456</div>
  <h1>Growing the money without breaking the floor</h1>
  <div class="sub">A daily equity/cash procedure for {{ M.W0 | musd(0) }} over {{ M.T_min_years | f(0) }}–{{ M.T_max_years | f(0) }} years
    with P(W<sub>T</sub> &lt; {{ M.K | musd(0) }}) ≤ {{ M.breach_target | pct(0) }} from any starting state</div>
  <div style="font-size:18px">Team 27: Arturo Favara, Clarys Vignal, Nick Bernardini</div>
  <div style="font-size:16px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:8px">23 November 2026</div>
</section>

<section class="slide">
  <div class="kicker">1 · Recommendation</div>
  <h1>Premium-robust DP: {{ H.adv_best_simple_min | bp }} to {{ H.adv_best_simple_max | bp }} bp/yr over the best simple rule, with worst-case floor breach ≤ {{ H.dp_worst_max | pct }} in every starting state.</h1>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col" style="flex:0.55">
      <div class="big">{{ H.dp_ce_min | pct(1, true) }} to {{ H.dp_ce_max | pct(1, true) }}</div>
      <div class="bigl">CE − cash per year (annualised), us_mkt, by starting state and horizon</div>
      <div class="big">≤ {{ H.dp_worst_max | pct }}</div>
      <div class="bigl">worst-case breach over {{ S.robust_set | length }} models in each of {{ H.n_cells }} state × horizon cells (limit {{ M.breach_target | pct(0) }})</div>
      <div class="box">Fallback rule: assets with weak model diagnostics get gap-aware CPPI ({{ N.deploy.n_to_cppi }} of {{ N.deploy.n_assets }}: {{ N.deploy.to_cppi | names }}).</div>
    </div>
    <div class="col wide">
      {{ T_exec_html }}
      <div class="note">Each cell: base breach / worst-case breach / breach with zero premium (%) · <b>CE − cash (%/yr)</b>.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="src">Source: scripts/07_report_numbers.py → results/report/numbers.json (headline), tables/exec_compact_us_mkt.csv</div>
</section>

<section class="slide">
  <div class="kicker">2 · How it works</div>
  <h1>The DP holds equity only when one bad day cannot reach the floor: it de-risks near the floor and in high volatility.</h1>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col wide"><img src="{{ fig('policy') }}"></div>
    <div class="col" style="flex:0.75">
      <ul>
        <li><b>Near the floor</b> the equity weight falls as the cushion thins.</li>
        <li><b>In high volatility</b> it cuts equity even with a large cushion (φ = {{ N.policy.phi_y15_normal | f(2) }} → {{ N.policy.phi_y15_crisis | f(2) }} at y = 1.5, normal → crisis σ).</li>
        <li><b>Robust to a halved premium</b>: the breach penalty λ is calibrated against μ × {{ S.mu_low_mult | f(1) }} as well as five models.</li>
        <li>The floor is discounted at a <b>conservative rate</b> (the {{ S.floor_alpha | pct(1) }} quantile of cash growth), which covers reinvestment risk.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="src">Source: scripts/07_report_numbers.py → results/report/inputs/policy_us_mkt.npz (results/policies/dp_premrobust_us_mkt.npz)</div>
</section>

<section class="slide">
  <div class="kicker">3 · The floor holds from every start</div>
  <h1>Worst-case breach stays below {{ H.dp_worst_max | pct }} from calm to the 1987-crash state, at both horizons.</h1>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col wide"><img src="{{ fig('heatmap') }}"></div>
    <div class="col" style="flex:0.6">
      <ul>
        <li>Worst case = maximum over the base model, GARCH-t, filtered historical simulation, parameter draws and persistent vol.</li>
        <li>{{ S.n_paths_eval | i }} paths per cell on a seed independent of tuning: SE at 2% ≈ {{ S.mc_se_2pct_50k | pp(2) }} pp.</li>
        <li>Gap-aware CPPI: ≤ {{ H.cg_worst_max | pct }}; OBPI: ≤ {{ H.ob_worst_max | pct }}.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="src">Source: scripts/07_report_numbers.py → results/report/tables/all_cells.csv</div>
</section>

<section class="slide">
  <div class="kicker">4 · Stress tests and other assets</div>
  <h1>Held-out stresses pass except fat tails (ν = {{ S.fat_nu_min }}) from crisis starts; on other assets the deployed strategy's worst case stays ≤ {{ N.ind.deployed_worst_max | pct }}.</h1>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col wide"><img src="{{ fig('stress') }}"></div>
    <div class="col" style="flex:0.62">
      <ul style="font-size:16px">
        <li>Zero premium: DP max {{ N.stress.dp.mu_zero | pct }}. Fat tails: DP fails in {{ N.stress.n_fail["Premium-robust DP"] }} cells, gap-aware CPPI in {{ N.stress.n_fail["Gap-aware CPPI"] }}.</li>
        <li>{{ N.deploy.n_assets }} assets, each with its own estimates. The rule sends {{ N.deploy.to_cppi | names }} to CPPI.</li>
        {% if N.ind.n_dp_misses %}<li>The DP's {{ N.ind.n_dp_misses }} industry miss{{ "es" if N.ind.n_dp_misses > 1 else "" }} ({% for m in N.ind.dp_misses %}{{ m.asset | name }} {{ m.state }} T={{ m.T }}, {{ m.scenario }} {{ m.breach | pct }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}): {{ N.ind.n_dp_misses_caught }} caught by the rule.</li>{% endif %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="src">Source: scripts/07_report_numbers.py → results/report/tables/stress_us_mkt.csv, industries.csv, results/deployment.csv</div>
</section>

<section class="slide">
  <div class="kicker">5 · Limits and advice</div>
  <h1>Use it on long, clean histories with daily trading; switch to the CPPI fallback when the premium or the model is in doubt.</h1>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col">
      <div style="font-weight:700;margin-bottom:8px">Do not rely on it when…</div>
      <ul style="font-size:17px">
        <li>crashes beyond the data are plausible (ν = {{ S.fat_nu_min }}: up to {{ N.stress.dp.fat_tails | pct }} from extreme starts, T = 1);</li>
        <li>the premium may be near zero (margin only {{ N.stress.dp_mu_zero_min_margin | pp(2) }} pp in the tightest cell);</li>
        <li>the asset's diagnostics are flagged, or its history is short or broken;</li>
        <li>rates may move sharply: the DP holds the rate fixed ({{ N.decomp_dp.T2.rate | pct(0) }} of T = 2 breaches are rate-driven);</li>
        <li>daily trading can fail: halts, overnight gaps, real costs.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
      <div style="font-weight:700;margin-bottom:8px">Our advice</div>
      <ul style="font-size:17px">
        <li>Re-estimate at least annually; run the deployment diagnostics before every switch-on.</li>
        <li>Add a horizon-matched zero-coupon bond: it removes reinvestment risk and the conservative discount.</li>
        <li>Next: the rate as a DP state, a DP backtest with re-solves, DP validation on every asset.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="src">Source: scripts/07_report_numbers.py → results/report/numbers.json (stress, decomp_dp)</div>
</section>
</body></html>
